cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PlaySplat in your work, please cite the Web3D 2026 paper below
  rather than the repository itself.
title: PlaySplat
abstract: >-
  A browser-based system that turns a 3D Gaussian Splatting scene from something
  you view into something you play. Pointer and hand tracking share one gesture
  grammar, any capture can be dropped into the page, three co-registered
  representations deform together in shared object space, and the derived layers
  export to validated OpenUSD from the browser.
type: software
# Software contributors. The paper below carries a single author because ACM
# does not permit adding authors after acceptance, but the codebase credit is
# separate and reflects who worked on it.
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Danci
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6646-5531"
    affiliation: Savannah College of Art and Design
  - family-names: Kongsakulvatanasook
    given-names: Itim
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9374-7729"
    affiliation: Savannah College of Art and Design
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/omolism/PlaySplat"
url: "https://playsplats.com"
keywords:
  - 3D Gaussian Splatting
  - WebGL
  - OpenUSD
  - hand tracking
  - playable experience

preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
    From Viewing to Playing: Bring-Your-Own-Scene Interaction for 3D Gaussian
    Splatting on the Web
  authors:
